FUN_004431e8: initialize the stack fd with the ORIGINAL's deterministic leftovers

v2 of the former zero-init patch. The car-grid init consumes fd fields the
per-level setters never write, and publishes the whole block into car_fd. The
original's values there are leftovers of its (deterministic) call chain --
captured from the reference via tools/refinit.sh. Bisect proves fd[2]
(0x0041677c, a return address into dd2h code) is what steers the first
Track_Follow onto the reference's camera start strip: with it, our
recorded_strips_ matches the original exactly (0xfee0,0xfe84,0xfe28,...);
zeros settled two strips short (0xff98). Values are binary-determined, hence
faithful; fd[1] is the caller's stack address (environment-dependent, publishes
transiently into car_fd before Map_Height overwrites it) -- replicated as
captured so car_fd byte-compares clean against the wine reference.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -31674,6 +31674,22 @@
